# Test fixtures under tests/data hold exact codec bytes (e.g. GBK sample_gbk.log,
# where a bare 0x0A separates lines). With core.autocrlf=true on Windows git would
# otherwise rewrite those 0x0A to 0x0D0A on checkout, changing file size and
# breaking the tests' byte-for-byte idempotency check. Mark them binary.
crates/lumelog-core/tests/data/** binary

# Rust/TypeScript source and docs: normalize to LF in the repo.
*.rs text eol=lf
*.ts text eol=lf
*.md text
